  "guide": {
    "title": "User guide",
    "intro": "A quick overview of every section of NexusHub CRM: what it's for and how to use it.",
    "dashboard_body": "The big picture: total clients, appointments this week, tasks due, and pipeline value. The first place to check every morning.",
    "clients_body": "Your client records: create new profiles, add tags, enable portal access, chat with the client, and attach documents right from the record. You can also bulk-import clients from CSV, JSON, or XML with the \"Import\" button.",
    "contacts_body": "A general phonebook (clients, suppliers, colleagues): handy for contacts who aren't full clients yet. You can auto-import contacts already present among your clients.",
    "pipeline_body": "Sales deals organized into columns (stages): drag a deal from one stage to the next as the sale progresses.",
    "calendar_body": "Appointments and meetings: create new events linked to a client. Meeting requests sent by clients from their portal appear here labeled \"Client request\" and need to be confirmed or rejected.",
    "tasks_body": "Reminders and to-dos, with an optional due date: mark as done once completed.",
    "automations_body": "Automatic rules (e.g. send a message when a deal changes stage) and reusable blueprints to automate repetitive workflows.",
    "whatsapp_body": "WhatsApp message hub: send and receive messages with clients, manage reusable message templates.",
    "email_body": "Email campaigns and automated sequences (e.g. welcome emails, reminders) to your clients.",
    "chat_body": "Slack-style internal chat between team members, organized into channels. Separate from chat with individual clients, which lives on each client's record instead.",
    "accounting_body": "The accounting module: create invoices (draft → issued → paid), record journal entries, and check an always-current balance sheet and income statement. Every issued or paid invoice automatically posts the matching accounting entries.",
    "settings_body": "Your profile, company data, team, interface colors (white-label), notifications, Google Calendar integration, and your subscription plan.",
    "portal_body": "The client portal (accessible to your clients with dedicated credentials) lets them see their own appointments and tasks, chat with you, view shared documents, and book a meeting on their own."
  },
